{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-48115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following functions has a removable discontinuity at $x=3?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-48115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function $q(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=3.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have\n\n- $q(3)=0\\,$  exists  $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}q(x)=1$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}q(x)\\ne q(3)$  $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=3$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/d7fc2426919c72ff934d19e98eb7465b8a42852407809d242213da9c26a4ed4a.png)\n\n   \n\nNotice that the functions $h(x)$ and $p(x)$ are continuous at $x=3,$ while $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ both have a discontinuity at $x=3$ but they are *not* removable." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-48115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f3fa4efa22fce0b97d0b77d07860e5b5303e13e3efeeaf68824fdb791435e57c"} {"question" "q-48115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-48115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/1e4dbe85f96242b6bd813205681cc870275296b4b0d742362c6d8c3f759171b9.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/bb9aa283af3ca5001829d6c94e0a918bea169036e624d0b057d841eb607405c4.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/d685febffc35e662794856af66b08a934bbb05a9dcefad5c6a4cb955ec50d17a.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/d7fc2426919c72ff934d19e98eb7465b8a42852407809d242213da9c26a4ed4a.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/faf9b5fd5e5803f3c48792d9194cc98343b29ee34f2700322e7d112fc4a6c730.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-48115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/d7fc2426919c72ff934d19e98eb7465b8a42852407809d242213da9c26a4ed4a.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-47559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/613eaf413822013885a22df61a4bf32f7cd763bf11db71ab7b8769e19c0369b0.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- It has a removable discontinuity at $x=0.$\n- It is continuous at $x=3.$\n- It has removable discontinuities at both $x=0$ and $x=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-47559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function has a discontinuity at $x=0.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(0)=1$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)=2$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)\\ne f(0)$ $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=0$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nIn the same way, the function has a discontinuity at $x=3.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(3)=1$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=-2$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)\\ne f(3)$ $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=3$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, I and III are true while II is false." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-47559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f3fa4efa22fce0b97d0b77d07860e5b5303e13e3efeeaf68824fdb791435e57c"} {"question" "q-47559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-47559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-47559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-104387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following functions has a removable discontinuity at $x=-1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-104387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=1.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(-1)=-3$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)=1$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)\\ne f(-1)$ $\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=-1$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/340443e20bc285d2e711b81608a60eb81ff33537ece23860b11871f5373dfde2.png)\n\nNotice that the functions $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ are continuous at $x=-1,$ while $g(x)$ and $h(x)$ both have a discontinuity at $x=-1$ but they are *not* removable." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-104387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f3fa4efa22fce0b97d0b77d07860e5b5303e13e3efeeaf68824fdb791435e57c"} {"question" "q-104387" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-104387" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/340443e20bc285d2e711b81608a60eb81ff33537ece23860b11871f5373dfde2.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/b77c43e9e33a958c65d6b3478b50c2f43e56d4a514bd092b50a9856d353a78f5.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/c6c9826ddd0cfc64cfa288b365c20c2e8bd67398f8f049a3ff80db13ab979d3f.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/e82c2ab5ec147cbf2f6a6370aa10caaf23effdd672a2496add4bd72d2e5a9ab9.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/f1b1db6867e4629ba3155f5de1d59cdf36ed9190dbd7a18733bcbcf2f10402c5.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-104387" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/340443e20bc285d2e711b81608a60eb81ff33537ece23860b11871f5373dfde2.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-47516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/4e796ff4d915d8c8b829574ade4eab05c7740de1f376d00900ec0d14b08f97d9.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- It has a removable discontinuity at $x=-1.$\n- It has a removable discontinuity at $x=1.$\n- There are removable discontinuities at both $x=-1$ and $x=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-47516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is continuous at $x=-1.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(-1)=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)=f(-1)$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\nOn the other hand, the function has a discontinuity at $x=1.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(1)=1$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)\\ne f(1)$ $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=1$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, II is true while I and III are false." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-47516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f3fa4efa22fce0b97d0b77d07860e5b5303e13e3efeeaf68824fdb791435e57c"} {"question" "q-47516" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-47516" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-47516" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-48111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following functions has a removable discontinuity at $x=2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-48111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function $p(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=2.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $p(2)=2$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 2}p(x)=1$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 2}p(x)\\ne p(2)$ $\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=2$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/fbc65d4168ce2f6747e75a606b3ccc175f9a68d98f718e473255f085d929c334.png)\n\n  \n\nNotice that the functions $h(x)$ and $q(x)$ are continuous at $x=2,$ while $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ both have a discontinuity at $x=2$ but they are *not* removable." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-48111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f3fa4efa22fce0b97d0b77d07860e5b5303e13e3efeeaf68824fdb791435e57c"} {"question" "q-48111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-48111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/5c22017c6a89ddb6a4ff481de6b210e272075ca2e7d492785d4be4950982cce0.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/937d91014870e27a93c247e87b7008f5c63807df764503fc7a9ebccfa8044d65.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/bbe9ecff2a793d2cadb42c6dedfab841869fae3215f6da0d8b6da7b9fbfa4ec1.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/ebef782bf2d2df29c0b016e5f2e3ae42eab200f3ae502d1eea7fe522ff0f1b5a.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/fbc65d4168ce2f6747e75a606b3ccc175f9a68d98f718e473255f085d929c334.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-48111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/fbc65d4168ce2f6747e75a606b3ccc175f9a68d98f718e473255f085d929c334.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-48128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/e3fa6d490da81fca9b24f9de41b01daaa957f574375cc8523aec448a0ef73015.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above. For what values of $x$ does the function $y=f(x)$ have a removable discontinuity?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-48128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function has a discontinuity at $x=-2.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(-2)=0$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)}f(x)=1$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)}f(x)\\ne f(-2)\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=-2$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nNote that the function also has a discontinuity at $x=2.$ but it is not a point discontinuity. Checking the conditions, we find that\n\n- $f(2)=0$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ does not exist $\\,\\times $\n\nSo this time, the second condition failed, and therefore $x=2$ is not a point discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, the correct answer is $x=-2$ only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-48128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f3fa4efa22fce0b97d0b77d07860e5b5303e13e3efeeaf68824fdb791435e57c"} {"question" "q-48128" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-48128" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$x=-2$ and $x=2$ only"] ["text" "$x=-2$ only"] ["text" "$x=-3$ and $x=-2$ only"] ["text" "$x=-3$ and $x=2$ only"] ["text" "$x=2$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-48128" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=-2$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-104425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/assets/d869c61426504b7b24c2feebd60f68bca6f7dc8a2b40036bf5821e0208e1e197.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above. For what values of $x$ does the function $y=f(x)$ have a removable discontinuity?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-104425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function has a discontinuity at $x=2.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(2)=3$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=0$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)\\ne f(2)\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=2$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nThe function also has a discontinuity at $x=5.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(5)=-1$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 5}f(x)=2$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 5}f(x)\\ne f(5)\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=5$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nFinally,  the function has a discontinuity at $x=-1.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(-1)=3$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)$ does not exists $\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the second condition that failed, which tells us that $x=-1$ is not a removable discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, the correct answer is $x=2$ and $x=5$ only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-104425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f3fa4efa22fce0b97d0b77d07860e5b5303e13e3efeeaf68824fdb791435e57c"} {"question" "q-104425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040337/state.json" "file_sha256" "4370e383ebb56ec5bdf412eccb3a5b175804e36f1d6b6a69fab340f9fbb81662"} {"question" "q-104425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$x=-1$ and $x=2$ only"] ["text" "$x=-1$ and $x=5$ only"] ["text" "$x=2$ and $x=5$ only"] ["text" "$x=2$ only"] ["text" "$x=5$ only"]] "cate